  'rand-water-restricts-tshwane-supply-pretoria-east-2026-10-23',
  'Rand Water restricts Tshwane''s bulk water supply',
  'Utilities', '2026-10-23', 'Rekord', 'https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/local-news/2026/10/23/rand-water-limits-tshwane-supply-as-pretoria-reservoirs-hit-critical-levels/',
  'Rand Water has cut bulk water supply to Tshwane after the metro used more than its daily allocation, hitting reservoirs in Pretoria East.',
  'Rand Water told the City of Tshwane on 20 October that daily consumption in the metro had climbed to roughly 794 million litres, well above its 752-million-litre allocation. The utility said an immediate cut of 42 million litres a day was needed, rising to a 127-million-litre reduction over time. It warned that its system was running at full capacity and that supply could be restricted to any municipality still drawing beyond its share.

By 23 October the metro confirmed the cuts had reached Pretoria. A city spokesperson said Rand Water had restricted the flow into the Klapperkop and Garsfontein reservoirs, forcing Tshwane to apply flow control and cut outflow from both. Areas named as affected include Garsfontein, Elardus Park, Moreleta Park, Waterkloof Ridge, Monument Park, Constantia Park and Parkmore, where residents could see reduced pressure or brief interruptions, with normal flow taking longer to return to higher-lying streets. The metro has sent water tankers to help residents in the meantime.

An opposition Democratic Alliance councillor on the Tshwane council criticised the response, saying residents could wait days for a tanker to arrive and calling the situation unacceptable. The cuts coincide with a forecast of 31 to 35 degrees Celsius over the weekend, and residents in the affected suburbs have been asked to store drinking water, cut back on non-essential use such as watering gardens or washing cars, and expect taps to come back on at different times in different streets.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/news-headlines/local-news/2026/10/23/rand-water-limits-tshwane-supply-as-pretoria-reservoirs-hit-critical-levels/", "https://polity.org.za/article/rand-water-warns-of-looming-water-crisis-as-system-under-pressure-2026-10-20"]',
  'agent'
);
